# Line-ending discipline for the entire neohiro body.
#
# - All text files are checked out as LF on every platform.
# - The neohiro/check_eol.py doctor rule enforces this in CI.
# - A file marked binary is left alone regardless of its own bytes.
#
# To override per-file (e.g. a Windows-only .bat that genuinely needs CRLF),
# add a per-path override further down.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.bz2 binary
*.xz binary
*.7z binary
*.rar binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.avi binary
*.webm binary
*.age binary
*.key binary
*.pem binary

# Scripts that genuinely need CRLF (Windows-only line-noise)
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
